<title>USA: Telebras stock jumps.</title>
<headline>Telebras stock jumps.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stock of Brazilian telephone giant Telebras SA rose sharply Wednesday, one day after being battered by rumours that Brazil might devalue its currency.</p>
<p>Telebras' American Depositary Receipts shares jumped $8.50 to $143.50 in active trading of more than 5.1 million shares on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Telebras, a bellwether Brazilian stock, fell $11.25 Tuesday. Brazilian shares have been roiled by jitters that Brazil would devalue its currency, the real.</p>
<p>&quot;It probably was oversold yesterday. Basically there is no fundamental change in Latin America,&quot; said Lucia Skwarek, head of Latin American equities at UBS Securiities.</p>
</text>
